+    // "content://eu.faircode.xlua/" is NOT a real, declared authority - it only "works" on a rooted
+    // device where Xposed hooks the ContentProvider dispatch inside system_server and answers on
+    // behalf of Settings.System.CONTENT_URI. In a rootless/LSPatch build there is no such hook, so
+    // both that fake authority and Settings.System.CONTENT_URI resolve to nothing / the real settings
+    // provider and every query/call silently returns null (hence the empty Hooks list).
+    //
+    // The ONLY authority that is actually declared in the manifest and backed by a real ContentProvider
+    // running inside our own process is "eu.faircode.xlua.vxp" (see VXP.java). That is what must be used
+    // here for rootless operation.
+    public static Uri getURI() { return Uri.parse("content://eu.faircode.xlua.vxp/"); }
